`4878bbbe18149620fe290c6f988ea1aea4ff313bcf63675d14c781326cd352ea`.

The composed selector now admits exactly `llvm.ucmp.i32.i128` and
`llvm.scmp.i32.i128` with two named i128 operands in the existing SysV pair
locations `RDI:RSI` and `RDX:RCX`, and an i32 result. It compares the high
lanes first (signed or unsigned according to the intrinsic), then compares
equal-high low lanes unsigned. Existing compare, branch, setcc, shift, and add
instructions materialize -1/0/1 in EAX. A state-owned unique EAX join label
uses the verifier's established `generic_cfg_select_end` contract; neither the
machine instruction set, encoder, nor verifier changed.

Other intrinsic widths, wrong result or argument types, non-pair locations,
unsupported call envelopes, and `musttail` remain fail-closed. Permanent
coverage checks both exact intrinsic forms and i64/wrong-return near misses.
Executable coverage exercises equality, low-lane-only ordering, high-lane
ordering, unsigned maximum, signed minimum and maximum, and values where
signed and unsigned ordering disagree.

Fresh report-all moves exactly from 443 / 258 / 185 to 443 / 260 / 183. The
two expected rows disappear from the failure report with no collateral
emissions:

- `compiler_rt.cmp.__ucmpti2`;
- `compiler_rt.cmp.__cmpti2`.

A structured extraction containing exactly those two captured functions
emits a relocation-free ELF object with two global symbols. A pinned-Zig
`callconv(.c)` executable invokes both z_llvm rows for 12 precomputed i128
pairs, or 24 exact calls. The compiler_rt wrappers' expected ABI results
0/1/2 are checked directly.

